{"catalog_digest":"eb6c3e5035703837e44727d59a04bb2f3f746b4d0585bd9eaed5f0378f9531ef","composition_digest":"4f419cf9a5a1a35380ef9ce2dbf1452e9e1f8f137218053ac076174a389df77e","generation":"eb6c3e5035703837e44727d59a04bb2f3f746b4d0585bd9eaed5f0378f9531ef","system_text":{"composition_digest":"4f419cf9a5a1a35380ef9ce2dbf1452e9e1f8f137218053ac076174a389df77e","item_digest":"7ab356879bd31a5af7b0899ff5c41c2d85ea663f35ec05f032a94db23e934726","preflight_digest":"f427e20309a562a48858b9129cbe833006c315018957cd84cfab2d7ca57ab8d0","text":"## Magic Context\n\n`ctx_search` searches this project's archive — what earlier sessions said and decided, commits and notes; ask it before asking the user anything that may already be recorded, phrased as a question with the exact names in it. `ctx_memory` pins facts that stay true for the months this work lasts, for you and every agent on the project: what must not have to be found again, especially what cost you turns. They are not shown to you automatically; recall them with `ctx_search`. `ctx_note` is the tray for work you intend to return to, with its findings attached; findings without an intention are not a note; \"take a note\" from the user always goes there.","tool_names":["ctx_memory","ctx_note","ctx_search"]},"tools":[{"capabilities":["magic-context:notes/v1"],"description":"Session notes are pending intentions: work you intend to return to, with findings attached (\"take a note\" always qualifies). Not active steps, an executing plan, or restart insurance; a record of how things stand (world-state, a design at a point in time) with nothing you intend to do about it — that goes stale silently; a fact worth keeping is memory, the rest is nothing. First line = title (<80 chars). write saves; read lists rows (note_ids for bodies); update changes one; dismiss retires 1–50. Dismiss a note when its work lands or is abandoned; a queue you never dismiss from stops being read. surface_condition parks it until an outside check against repo files, git, GitHub or the web holds.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"action":{"description":"write | read | update | dismiss.","enum":["write","read","update","dismiss"],"type":"string"},"content":{"description":"Note text: first line title (<80 chars), then detail.","maxLength":65536,"type":"string"},"filter":{"description":"Read filter: all, active, pending, ready, dismissed. Omitted: active notes plus every current smart note (pending included); active: only active-status notes.","enum":["all","active","pending","ready","dismissed"],"type":"string"},"limit":{"default":25,"description":"Rows per read (default 25).","maximum":100,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"note_ids":{"description":"One id for update, 1–50 for dismiss, or 1–50 to read those notes in full. Write and a plain read take an empty list.","items":{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"maxItems":50,"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"offset":{"default":0,"description":"Skip newest rows (default 0).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"surface_condition":{"description":"A condition an outside checker can verify on its own, periodically (repository, releases, web — anything it can look up); never something only this conversation knows.","maxLength":4096,"type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"ctx_note","result_ops":["prepend","append"],"schema_digest":"f44043a45d8871421db70b4b94e838b684b9360ebc92017f201579a06ad0afd0","semantics":1},{"capabilities":["magic-context:memory.write/v1"],"description":"Durable facts about this project, shared with every agent on it and kept for the months this work lasts; active ones are already in <project-memory> as `#id: fact`. Write one standalone fact when it must not have to be found again — a rule, an architecture fact, a constraint, a config value, a naming convention — especially what cost you turns. A pending intention with evidence is ctx_note, not memory. write (content + category); update one id (content; category optional); archive one or more ids (reason optional); merge two or more ids (content); get 1–20 ids in any status.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"action":{"description":"write | update | archive | merge | get","enum":["write","update","archive","merge","get"],"type":"string"},"category":{"description":"Kind of fact (write; on update/merge pass the current category to keep it). Archive and get ignore it.","enum":["PROJECT_RULES","ARCHITECTURE","CONSTRAINTS","CONFIG_VALUES","NAMING"],"type":"string"},"content":{"description":"One standalone fact (write, update, merge). Archive and get: empty string.","maxLength":65536,"type":"string"},"ids":{"description":"Ids from <project-memory>: one for update, 1+ for archive, 2+ for merge, 1–20 for get. Write: empty list.","items":{"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"maxItems":100,"type":"array"},"reason":{"description":"Why it is archived (optional).","maxLength":4096,"type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"ctx_memory","result_ops":["prepend","append"],"schema_digest":"7a6a1d3f8c5e61d6104805e30e549c9d0e5172d023415a98cb225e0a6af89879","semantics":1},{"capabilities":["magic-context:archive.search/v1"],"description":"Search the archive — everything that ever happened here that is not on your desk: memories not in <project-memory>, compacted conversation, commits, notes. Phrase query as a natural-language question carrying the exact terms you expect (\"where is the opencode source code path?\", \"why did we choose SQLite over postgres?\", \"how does the dreamer lease work?\") — a keyword stack finds less. Sources (omit for all): memory (rules, conventions), message (compacted conversation; hits carry ordinals for ctx_expand), git_commit (when did this change), primer (reusable project Q&A the dreamer distils from recurring questions), note (parked follow-ups). Memory ids alone (`#7234`) resolve directly. from/to restrict every source to an inclusive UTC date range.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"from":{"description":"Earliest date, YYYY-MM-DD (inclusive).","type":"string"},"limit":{"default":10,"description":"Maximum results (default 10).","maximum":25,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"query":{"description":"A natural-language question carrying the exact terms you expect in the answer.","maxLength":1024,"type":"string"},"sources":{"description":"Restrict to these sources; omit or [] for all.","items":{"enum":["memory","message","git_commit","primer","note"],"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"to":{"description":"Latest date, YYYY-MM-DD (inclusive; default open).","type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"},"name":"ctx_search","result_ops":["prepend","append"],"schema_digest":"f0d56f456f2ee9569c030072d33a001ae45d8a57d792dbf4d51c59eb12da28e9","semantics":1}]}